  "solution": {
    "text": "Shape of XeF $\\rightarrow$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2017_che_a50.png\">\r\n\r\nThe Xe show $s p^{3} d^{3}$ -hybridisation in $XeF^{-}_{5}$, Thus, its geometry is Pentagonal-bipyramidal. But, number of electron pair $=\\frac{8+5+1}{2}=7$ Number of bond pair $=5^{2},$ number of lone pair $=2$ A lot of electrons are present at axil position and all bonds are in same plane. Hence, the shape is planar.",
